       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5,100 mg/day**. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2,550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's **2,000 mg/day**. This order is about twice the highest labeled dose, which raises the risk of severe GI side effects and lactic acidosis.\n\n**It may have been meant as one of these:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- Something else, such as 500 mg TID if the patient is just starting. Metformin is usually started low and increased gradually to limit GI side effects.\n\nCan you confirm which dose you want? I can enter it as soon as you reply. If you do mean 1,700 mg TID, please confirm and give the clinical reason, and I'll add a note to the order."
      }
